1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,305
Distributive Property. One multiplier — every term inside gets

2
00:00:04,305 --> 00:00:07,052
it. It's one of the most useful tricks in

3
00:00:07,052 --> 00:00:08,611
all of mathematics.

4
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:12,157
Imagine you're an ancient land surveyor. You have a

5
00:00:12,157 --> 00:00:15,212
large field divided into two sections: wheat on one

6
00:00:15,212 --> 00:00:17,860
side, corn on the other. You need to know

7
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:21,119
the total area. Do you measure the entire field?

8
00:00:21,119 --> 00:00:24,038
Or measure each section and add them? Both give

9
00:00:24,038 --> 00:00:26,618
the same answer — that's our story today.

10
00:00:26,983 --> 00:00:30,897
Watch this carefully. Here's the whole field. Now let

11
00:00:30,897 --> 00:00:33,924
me split it into two pieces. The yellow piece

12
00:00:33,924 --> 00:00:36,509
and the green piece. If I add them back

13
00:00:36,509 --> 00:00:39,831
together, do I get the same total? Yes! The

14
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:42,194
whole equals the sum of the parts.

15
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:46,003
Let me show you this idea with letters. Let's

16
00:00:46,003 --> 00:00:49,624
call the height of our rectangle 'a'. The width

17
00:00:49,624 --> 00:00:52,488
of the yellow part is 'b', and the width

18
00:00:52,488 --> 00:00:55,267
of the green part is 'c'. The area of

19
00:00:55,267 --> 00:00:58,467
the whole rectangle is a times (b plus c).

20
00:00:58,467 --> 00:01:00,993
The area of the yellow part is a times

21
00:01:00,993 --> 00:01:03,773
b, and the green part is a times c.

22
00:01:03,773 --> 00:01:08,068
So: a(b+c) equals ab plus ac. That's the distributive

23
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:12,194
property over addition. The same idea also works over

24
00:01:12,194 --> 00:01:15,310
subtraction: a times (b minus c) equals a b

25
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:16,321
minus a c.

26
00:01:16,683 --> 00:01:20,195
Let's try this with real numbers. What is 4

27
00:01:20,195 --> 00:01:25,057
times 23? Instead of multiplying directly, break 23 into

28
00:01:25,057 --> 00:01:27,578
20 and 3. So we have 4 times (20

29
00:01:27,578 --> 00:01:31,360
plus 3). Distribute the 4: 4 times 20 equals

30
00:01:31,360 --> 00:01:34,782
80, and 4 times 3 equals 12. Add them:

31
00:01:34,782 --> 00:01:39,284
80 plus 12 equals 92. That's the distributive property

32
00:01:39,284 --> 00:01:44,236
over addition. Now let's try one over subtraction. What

33
00:01:44,236 --> 00:01:46,847
is 6 times 98? Think of 98 as 100

34
00:01:46,847 --> 00:01:49,909
minus 2. So we have 6 times (100 minus

35
00:01:49,909 --> 00:01:53,960
2). Distribute the 6: 6 times 100 equals 600,

36
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:57,652
and 6 times 2 equals 12. Subtract them: 600

37
00:01:57,652 --> 00:02:02,334
minus 12 equals 588. Same trick, works either way!

38
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:06,737
Here's a mistake many students make. When solving 4

39
00:02:06,737 --> 00:02:10,258
times (20 plus 3), some multiply only the first

40
00:02:10,258 --> 00:02:13,264
term. They write 4 times 20, plus 3 —

41
00:02:13,264 --> 00:02:17,472
forgetting to multiply the second term! That gives 80

42
00:02:17,472 --> 00:02:20,650
plus 3, which is 83 — and that's wrong.

43
00:02:20,650 --> 00:02:24,515
Remember: the 4 must multiply every term inside the

44
00:02:24,515 --> 00:02:28,208
brackets. The correct way is 4 times 20, plus

45
00:02:28,208 --> 00:02:32,073
4 times 3, which gives 92. Always distribute to

46
00:02:32,073 --> 00:02:33,791
every single term!

47
00:02:34,150 --> 00:02:39,039
Subtraction has its own tricky mistake. When solving 6

48
00:02:39,039 --> 00:02:43,341
times the quantity 100 minus 2, some students flip

49
00:02:43,341 --> 00:02:47,056
the sign. They write 6 times 100, plus 6

50
00:02:47,056 --> 00:02:50,576
times 2 — turning the minus into a plus!

51
00:02:50,576 --> 00:02:53,704
That gives 600 plus 12, which is 612 —

52
00:02:53,704 --> 00:02:58,593
and that's wrong. Remember: the minus sign must stay

53
00:02:58,593 --> 00:03:03,677
between the two distributed products. The correct way is

54
00:03:03,677 --> 00:03:07,295
6 times 100, minus 6 times 2, which gives

55
00:03:07,295 --> 00:03:11,597
588. Keep the operation exactly as it was inside

56
00:03:11,597 --> 00:03:13,161
the brackets!

57
00:03:13,517 --> 00:03:17,365
Here's a real-world example. 5 friends each buy a

58
00:03:17,365 --> 00:03:19,930
notebook for 20 rupees and a pen for 3

59
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:23,864
rupees. What's the total cost? We can think of

60
00:03:23,864 --> 00:03:26,600
it as 5 times (20 plus 3). Or, buy

61
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:30,277
all 5 notebooks first: 100 rupees. Then all 5

62
00:03:30,277 --> 00:03:36,263
pens: 15 rupees. Total: 115 rupees. Distribution happens naturally

63
00:03:36,263 --> 00:03:37,888
in everyday life!

64
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:42,276
Time to try one yourself: seven times nineteen. Here's

65
00:03:42,276 --> 00:03:45,605
a hint — nineteen equals twenty minus one. Take

66
00:03:45,605 --> 00:03:48,005
a moment here and work it out using the

67
00:03:48,005 --> 00:03:49,941
distributive property.

68
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:04,325
Seven times nineteen becomes seven times the quantity twenty

69
00:04:04,325 --> 00:04:07,488
minus one, which splits into one hundred forty minus

70
00:04:07,488 --> 00:04:11,476
seven, giving one hundred thirty three. Quick mental math,

71
00:04:11,476 --> 00:04:13,401
all thanks to distributing.

72
00:04:13,767 --> 00:04:18,168
Remember: the distributive property is just breaking things apart.

73
00:04:18,168 --> 00:04:21,262
Wherever you see a(b+c), you can distribute — split

74
00:04:21,262 --> 00:04:24,632
the parts, multiply each, then add them back. Use

75
00:04:24,632 --> 00:04:28,139
it for mental math, and for real-life shopping. Break

76
00:04:28,139 --> 00:04:29,858
it down to make it simple.

77
00:04:30,217 --> 00:04:33,993
Let's recap the power of breaking it apart. Over

78
00:04:33,993 --> 00:04:37,341
addition: a times open bracket b plus c close

79
00:04:37,341 --> 00:04:41,118
bracket equals a b plus a c. Over subtraction:

80
00:04:41,118 --> 00:04:44,208
a times open bracket b minus c close bracket

81
00:04:44,208 --> 00:04:46,611
equals a b minus a c. We used it

82
00:04:46,611 --> 00:04:50,131
for quick mental math, and for splitting a real

83
00:04:50,131 --> 00:04:54,251
shopping bill. Whenever a number multiplies a sum or

84
00:04:54,251 --> 00:04:58,285
a difference, you can distribute it across every term

85
00:04:58,285 --> 00:05:01,375
— break it down to make it simple. Thank

86
00:05:01,375 --> 00:05:04,293
you so much for watching, and I will see

87
00:05:04,293 --> 00:05:06,268
you in the next lesson!
